<title>MEXICO: Acer Peripherals to invest in Mexico.</title>
<headline>Acer Peripherals to invest in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acer Peripherals Inc, a subsidiary of Taiwanese computer maker Acer Inc, said Firday it would invest $230 million in two projects in Mexico starting next year.</p>
<p>&quot;These investments consolidate the commitment Acer has with Mexico and with the markets of Latin America,&quot; Stan Shih, president of the company, said at a news conference.</p>
<p>The first project, worth $80 million, will involve the contruction of a plant to make computer monitors. It is scheduled to begin production in July 1997.</p>
<p>The other, a $150 plant to make mother boards and other parts, is due to start operating in 1998, Shih said.</p>
<p>--Maria Luisa Aguilar, Mexico City newsroom, (525) 728-9553</p>
</text>
